{"number": 145, "text": "                              pairs\n            If you have problems in hearing the difference between individual sounds in Section A of the\n            book, you  will be directed to one of the exercises in this section.\n\n            or\n            Look  in D3 Guide for speakers of specific languages, find the sound pairs recommended for\n            speakers of your language, and do these.\n            In order to remember which  sound pairs you have done, put a tick in the boxes. If you have\n            completed  it but you still find it difficult, tick ‘visited’. If you are sure you know it, tick\n            ‘understood’. If you have recorded yourself saying the words correctly, tick ‘recorded’.\n\n            Sound     pair  1: /a/  and   /e/\n            For more  on these sounds, see Units 2, 6.                   man  — men     had = head\n            Listen to the words in the box.                               gas—guess           said\n            Listen. The speaker will say two words from the box.\n            If you hear the same word twice, write S (same).\n            If you hear two different words, write D (different).\n                         De                       4.\n            Listen. Circle the word you hear.\n              8 bad | bed\n              9 dad/ dead\n             10     set\n             11 marry / merry\n             12 Talk to the man / men.\n\n            Sound     pair  2: /a@/ and   /a/\n            For more  on these sounds, see Units 2, 18.\n                                                                           ran—run         — cut\n             Listen to the words in the box.                                             sang — sung\n             Listen. The speaker will say two words from the box.\n             If you hear the same word twice, write S (same).\n             If you hear two different words, write D (different).\n\n\n             Listen. Circle the word you hear.\n      